{"parents": [{"link": "../", "title": "Available Methods"}], "prev": {"link": "../answer_callback_query/", "title": "answer_callback_query()"}, "next": {"link": "../set_bot_commands/", "title": "set_bot_commands()"}, "title": "request_callback_answer()", "meta": null, "body": "<section id=\"request-callback-answer\">\n<h1>request_callback_answer()<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#request-callback-answer\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyrogram.Client.request_callback_answer\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">Client.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">request_callback_answer</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#pyrogram.Client.request_callback_answer\" title=\"Link to this definition\">\u00b6</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Request a callback answer from bots.\nThis is the equivalent of clicking an inline button containing callback data.</p>\n<strong>Usable by</strong>\n<span class=\"usable-by\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-check\" style=\"color: var(--color-green)\"></i> Users</span>\n<span class=\"usable-by\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-xmark\" style=\"color: var(--color-red)\"></i> Bots</span><dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>chat_id</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></code> | <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></code>) \u2013 Unique identifier (int) or username (str) of the target chat.\nFor your personal cloud (Saved Messages) you can simply use \u201cme\u201d or \u201cself\u201d.\nFor a contact that exists in your Telegram address book you can use his phone number (str).</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>message_id</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></code>) \u2013 The message id the inline keyboard is attached on.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>callback_data</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></code> | <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">bytes</span></code>) \u2013 Callback data associated with the inline button you want to get the answer from.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>password</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></code>, <em>optional</em>) \u2013 When clicking certain buttons (such as BotFather\u2019s confirmation button to transfer ownership), if your account has 2FA enabled, you need to provide your account\u2019s password.\nThe 2-step verification password for the current user. Only applicable, if the <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../../types/InlineKeyboardButton/#pyrogram.types.InlineKeyboardButton\" title=\"pyrogram.types.InlineKeyboardButton\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">InlineKeyboardButton</span></code></a> contains <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">callback_data_with_password</span></code>.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>timeout</strong> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></code>, <em>optional</em>) \u2013 Timeout in seconds.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>The answer containing info useful for clients to display a notification at the top of the chat screen\nor as an alert.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Raises<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#TimeoutError\" title=\"(in Python v3.14)\"><strong>TimeoutError</strong></a> \u2013 In case the bot fails to answer within 10 seconds.</p></li>\n<li><p><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.14)\"><strong>ValueError</strong></a> \u2013 In case of invalid arguments.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>RPCError</strong> \u2013 In case of Telegram RPC error.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-python notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"k\">await</span> <span class=\"n\">app</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">request_callback_answer</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">chat_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">message_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;callback_data&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n", "metatags": "<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n", "rellinks": [["genindex", "General Index", "I", "index"], ["py-modindex", "Python Module Index", "", "modules"], ["api/methods/set_bot_commands", "set_bot_commands()", "N", "next"], ["api/methods/answer_callback_query", "answer_callback_query()", "P", "previous"]], "sourcename": "", "toc": "<ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#\">request_callback_answer()</a><ul>\n<li><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyrogram.Client.request_callback_answer\"><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Client.request_callback_answer()</span></code></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n", "display_toc": true, "page_source_suffix": ".rst", "current_page_name": "api/methods/request_callback_answer", "sidebars": ["sidebar/brand.html", "sidebar/search.html", "sidebar/scroll-start.html", "sidebar/navigation.html", "sidebar/scroll-end.html"], "alabaster_version": "1.0.0", "alabaster_version_info": [1, 0, 0], "furo_version": "2025.12.19", "furo_navigation_tree": "", "furo_hide_toc": false, "furo_pygments": {"light": {"background": "#eeffcc", "foreground": "black"}, "dark": {"background": "#202020", "foreground": "#d0d0d0"}}}